From e0d69d1e301b06694ceec6e07b33cfae3bc5ad4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:10:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10191/11362] Retract 25 stale flagged_adversarial stamps; 133
 are blocked by a second defect

MEASURED. Of 5,844 result artifacts, 567 carry flagged_adversarial: True.
Re-running today's gate over all 567 finds 366 still CRITICAL and 201 now
clean, zero errors -- confirming the 2026-08-25 figure of ~200 as a stable
standing population, not drift.

WHY they went clean was measured before anything was written, because it
decides whether retracting is safe. Recorded original reasons: 135
DURATION_TOO_SHORT, 102 METHODOLOGY_MISSING, 53 TAUTOLOGY, 22
IMPLAUSIBLE_PERFECT, 3 FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK. The dominant three map to
documented false-positive CORRECTIONS this project made deliberately -- the
Inference-Substrate Declaration Discipline's per-substrate duration floors
(exp2837/exp2842), the methodology skip for aggregation-only artifacts, and
the 2026-05-31 identifier/seed exclusion -- and both mechanisms are present in
the current gate.

SCOPE. 158 eligible: reason falls WHOLLY within those documented classes. Held
back untouched and verified still flagged True: 22 IMPLAUSIBLE_PERFECT (the
exp1851 fabrication class; no fix retired it, and several declare no
inference_substrate at all), 20 with no recorded reason, 1 mixed-kind.

ONLY 25 LANDED, AND THE REASON IS THE FINDING. 133 of the 158 could not be
committed because they carry a SECOND, pre-existing defect: they fail
scripts/arc_artifact_lint.py on INVALID_INFERENCE_SUBSTRATE, MISSING_
INFERENCE_SUBSTRATE, DURATION_MISSING or LIVE_LLM_NOT_ALLOWLISTED. Those
defects predate this change -- the substrate strings are byte-identical to HEAD
-- and every one of the 133 was restored to its stamped state rather than
landed half-corrected. Their stamps stay stale, honestly, pending a decision on
the underlying defect.

The wider population is measured in ops/known-issues.md: of 573 ARC candidate
artifacts, 194 declare an illegal inference_substrate and 141 declare none --
335 of 573, about 58%, would fail the moment they were staged. The guard has
been green because nothing re-stages write-once artifacts, the same structural
blind spot CLAUDE.md documents for operator_curated_docs_lint.

METHOD. --backfill was the wrong tool; it only ADDS stamps to artifacts
critical now and unstamped. Retraction uses the route
determination_preservation_lint.py documents, whose worked example is this
exact case: keep the field, set it false, add flagged_adversarial_cleared_note
beside it. Each artifact was re-verified INDIVIDUALLY at write time rather than
trusting the sweep's cached verdict. Nothing was deleted: the original stamp
and every corrigendum_pending entry are preserved, and the note says so.

experiment_5895_shortcut_safe_continuous_self_learning.json is mode 444, a
deliberate write-protection, and was left alone rather than chmod-ed to tidy a
sweep. No entry was added to SUBSTRATE_DURATION_FLOORS to make this commit
pass; that is what substrate_alias_evidence_lint exists to catch.

Verified: flagged_adversarial absent from 0 artifacts, 26 of 26 carry the
retraction note, determination-preservation-lint OK, arc-artifact-lint exit 0
on the staged set.

